description:
A junior firmware engineer wrote a function to update a 4-bit field in bits [7:4] of a 16-bit register.

```c
uint16_t set_field_BUGGY(uint16_t reg, uint8_t val) {
    uint16_t mask = 0x00F0;
    reg = reg & mask;             // Bug 1: wipes out all bits outside [7:4]!
    reg |= (val << 4);            // Bug 2: unmasked val clobbers bits [15:8]!
    return reg;
}
```
### Tasks:
Implement `set_field_fixed(reg, val)` resolving both bugs:
1. Clear only the target field using bitwise NOT `~mask`.
2. Mask `val & 0x0F` before shifting to ensure no overflow into adjacent register fields.
